  "analysis": "The terminal keeps truncating long outputs. I can see rules.json has the models (cheap, default, pro, ultra), thresholds, signals for daily reports and heavy keywords, and response policies. State.json has mode and feedback counts. I need to see the full router.py implementation.",
  "plan": "Let me try reading router.py in smaller chunks using head and tail with specific line counts, and save the content to a temp file to analyze.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -80 skill_context/router.py > /tmp/r1.txt && cat /tmp/r1.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '81,160p' skill_context/router.py > /tmp/r2.txt && cat /tmp/r2.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '161,240p' skill_context/router.py > /tmp/r3.txt && cat /tmp/r3.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
